<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Killarney</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Killarney is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kerry">County Kerry</a> in south-west Ireland, beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-leane">Lough Leane</a> and the lakes and mountains of Killarney National Park. The surrounding district was the early medieval centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganacht</a> Locha Léin kings of Iarmumu, with the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inisfallen">Inisfallen</a> and later Ross Castle. It grew into a tourist resort from the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/killarney.jpg" alt="Killarney" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marathon · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Mary%27s_Cathedral,_Killarney_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7872794.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
